 "differences": [
  "The 62 people of E1b are also E1 participants of Vandevoorde2020_JNeurophysiol (identical hand angles in trials 261-622); that release also has their dual-task baseline reaches. Drop one of the two when pooling datasets. ",
  "The E1b ANOVA (F(1,58) = 2.49 in the paper) is not used as a check: it has 58 error df, so the authors analysed 61 of the 62 people, and the exclusion is not documented. The paper gives mean ages (22.75 and 66.88 y) but the deposit only has young or older, so these cannot be checked.",
  "The paper says reaches with angular errors above 60 deg were removed before processing, but 285 hand angles (0.2 percent) in the deposit lie beyond 60 deg (up to 270 deg); they are kept as shared."
 ],
